The implicit conversion of string to integer "bug" has occurred before:

- https://github.com/jekyll/jekyll/issues/3414
- https://github.com/jekyll/jekyll/issues/8653

It looks like users want to be able to filter `site.data` to find arbitrary properties, instead of only specified properties. People expect `site.data` to be an object with properties, instead of an indexed array.

Say we're looking for a file in `site.data` whose name is in `page.json_filename`. 

I think this is the only method that works: 

```
{% for data in site.data %}
{% if data[0] == page.json_filename %}
{{ data[1] | inspect }}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
```
